  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **The in-memory layer, `SqliteMemoryDbPoolSqlLayer`, lets the pools on a machine create up to 1000 databases,** where every layer allowed 100: an in-memory database costs memory only while a pool holds it, and is private to that pool. Compze's own test suite held 152 at once on a machine with 32 logical processors, and with 100 its tests timed out waiting for a free database.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.DbPool 0.4.0-alpha (was 0.3.0-alpha), Compze.Sql.Sqlite 0.8.1-alpha (was 0.5.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
